        fb="🌡️ The cheapest heating zoning system ever invented is already half-fitted in most houses: the TRV.\n\nThose numbered valves on your radiators let every room run its own temperature. Spare room you use twice a month? Setting 1–2. Living room? 3–4. That's heat going only where you actually live.\n\n💷 The valves themselves are modest money, fitting is quick, and the saving compounds every single heating day.\n\nGot radiators with no TRVs at all — or ancient ones that don't really respond? That's an upgrade that quietly pays you back.",
