        gb="Thermostatic radiator valves are easy to overlook, but they're the cheapest room-by-room heating control available. Each numbered valve regulates its own radiator: a spare room that's rarely used can sit at setting 1–2 while the living room runs at 3–4, so you stop paying to heat rooms nobody is in. The valves are modest in cost, fitting is quick, and the saving repeats every day the heating runs. If some of your radiators have no TRVs at all — or older valves that have stiffened and no longer respond — upgrading them is one of the better-value improvements you can make to a heating system. Radiator and valve work across Southampton.",
