        gb="A recent diagnostic job in Shirley: a combi boiler kept cutting out with no fault code and no obvious pattern — exactly the kind of intermittent problem that becomes expensive when engineers start swapping parts on guesswork. The methodical route: multimeter on the thermistor while the boiler warmed through. The resistance readings drifted out of specification as temperatures rose, effectively telling the control board the water was boiling when it wasn't, so the boiler shut itself down, cooled, recovered and repeated the cycle. One sensor replaced, and it has behaved since. Proper diagnosis costs a little patience and saves a lot of parts. Boiler repairs across Southampton with a £100 diagnostic.",
